    {
      "v": 8,
      "zh": "萬 軍 之 耶 和 華 說 ， 在 顯 出 榮 耀 之 後 ， 差 遣 我 去 懲 罰 那 擄 掠 你 們 的 列 國 ， 摸 你 們 的 就 是 摸 他 眼 中 的 瞳 人 。",
      "en": "For the Lord of Heaven’s Armies says: “For his own glory[NOTE:1] he has sent me to the nations that plundered you—for anyone who touches you touches the pupil[NOTE:2] of his[NOTE:3] eye.[NOTE:4]",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “After glory has he sent me” (similar KJV, NASB). What is clearly in view is the role of Zechariah who, by faithful proclamation of the message, will glorify the Lord.",
        "Heb “gate” (בָּבָה, bavah) of the eye, that is, pupil. The rendering of this term by KJV as “apple” has created a well-known idiom in the English language, “the apple of his eye” (so ASV, NIV). The pupil is one of the most vulnerable and valuable parts of the body, so for Judah to be considered the “pupil” of the Lord’s eye is to raise her value to an incalculable price (cf. NLT “my most precious possession”).",
        "A scribal emendation (tiqqun sopherim) has apparently altered an original “my eye” to “his eye” in order to allow the prophet to be the speaker throughout vv. 8-9. This alleviates the problem of the Lord saying, in effect, that he has sent himself on the mission to the nations.",
        "Heb “I will wave my hand over them” (so NASB); NIV, NRSV “raise my hand against them.”"
      ],
